# say(); lay(); say(); take(); say()   with   say = () => { print(asks()); }   function asks() { return $isWithoutAddedNames(Object.prototype); }   as the library's own text may write it
# In a test run a test may lay a name above all objects where the build sees it do so: the record in front of the module. The library's short roads, which make no object that such a name would be found on, ask ONE BYTE:
# it says "as built" from where the holder hears of writes, and "added" for good from the first name that is laid, also when the name is taken away again.
# OPTIONS: admit=ReplacedBuiltins
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all const aboveAll = Object.prototype; globalThis.lay = () => { Object.defineProperty(aboveAll, "laid", { value: 1, configurable: true }); }; globalThis.take = () => { delete aboveAll.laid; };
# CHECK: true
# CHECK-NEXT: false
# CHECK-NEXT: false
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(FORM): walk f1 mechanisms=none
# FORM-LABEL: code f1:Body
# FORM: = IsHolderWithoutAddedNames builtin=ObjectPrototype

